# `m[k, or: start]` is a writable map slot. `counts[w, or: 0] += 1` counts
# words and `groups[n, or: fresh(n)].push(w)` groups them, each with one
# lookup; `fresh` runs once per missing key, never for a present one. A
# string slot appends to its start. A present key's compound assignment and
# a plain set never run the start. As a value the slot reads the stored
# value or the start and adds no entry, on an immutable map too. The same
# lines on O0, O1 and O2.
fixture: Fixtures/MapUpsertSlotLooksUpOnceAndStartsLazily
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = map_upsert_slot_looks_up_once_and_starts_lazily.out
stderr: empty
step: jet run -O1 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = map_upsert_slot_looks_up_once_and_starts_lazily.out
stderr: empty
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = map_upsert_slot_looks_up_once_and_starts_lazily.out
stderr: empty
